"test":{"name":"fog-rule-supply-transit-unseen","kind":"rules","opponent":"Human","rounds":"4","check":"supplyTransitUnseen","question":"Known unknowns for supply in transit (SupplyNetwork.UnseenContacts, SupplyContacts): under fog the screen shows the network and the supply line as they truly are, and where enemies its side does not see stop a transit or send it round, a contact marker says why: beside such an enemy, never on it, never on one of the side's units. Blue's HQ at (-6,0), a Blue supply unit in its supply at (-3,0) (the source the APC must reach), an APC carrying supplies at (2,0), Blue the screen's player. A line of Red grunts at x=-1 Blue does not see: cut off, truly and as shown, the APC unfed; a contact. Seen by a recon: still cut, no contact. A single unseen Red grunt beside the way (moves to spare): linked round it, the supply line the true way clear of it, one contact. With a Blue helicopter parked where that contact would go (it does not spot the stealthy grunt beside it), the contact goes beside it instead. No unseen enemy, or fog off: no contacts.","rules":"standard"},
